<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:59Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>BRICS Summit 2026: Putin, Modi reaffirm partnership</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63fbdd7e4840778d6a66b01901c07ae2db0fa41232469b61cca654063387dd91</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T12:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brics-summit-2026-putin-modi-reaffirm-partnership/live-79224239--ae45dba23a6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brics-summit-2026-putin-modi-reaffirm-partnership/live-79224239?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Modi will also meet Xi Jinping as India seeks to balance ties with China and Russia. The wars in Ukraine and Iran could test the group's unity at the summit. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war: Saudi-Houthi escalation intensifies Yemen conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6559b3b4fd41d3a23aff553acea0f60382eab022f22990d084c3a60a51c462d6</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T11:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-saudi-houthi-escalation-intensifies-yemen-conflict/a-79226627--c5b66c310724.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-saudi-houthi-escalation-intensifies-yemen-conflict/a-79226627?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Houthi takeovers of Mokha, Dhubab and Perim in the Bab el-Mandeb Strait threaten to push Yemen deeper into the Middle East war. The Iran-backed group has made advances against Yemen's government and Saudi Arabia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany charges 7 suspected Hamas members over attack plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4262f2047b055ee5cfe673b8f1e4ed5538ce7880e3886a6c5c2f8f071da3b58a</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T11:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-charges-7-suspected-hamas-members-over-attack-plot/a-79230171--a30b5fe0228d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-charges-7-suspected-hamas-members-over-attack-plot/a-79230171?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prosecutors say the suspects had moved beyond general preparations and were already pursuing a concrete plan for a deadly attack on Israeli or Jewish targets.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>9/11 conspiracy theories that continue to circulate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d072368185d5db49c0231844515dd6ed43ccf0f88f0bf33bde0453ace5f6df2</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/9-11-conspiracy-theories-that-continue-to-circulate/a-78896069--975de526f230.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/9-11-conspiracy-theories-that-continue-to-circulate/a-78896069?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter-century after the September 11, 2001, attacks, they are still the focus of numerous conspiracy theories. Why do people believe them?</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>India looks to steer BRICS away from anti-Western turn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:286234b624cb12fd43252b325b475cd010653ec49e719f372c57efa9dfe24018</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234--e9a076e9f28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The BRICS summit 2026 takes place in Delhi this weekend. Unlike last year, Putin and Xi are expected to attend. Can India keep the expanded bloc united?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why North Korea's Kim Jong Un doesn't need a US deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ec549c549b3ed62527323bc71edffb1e8f0637881a8c8423e14fc370835c678</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854--e7f102464964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's overtures to North Korea's dictator have gone nowhere, with an emboldened Pyongyang accelerating its nuclear program and solidifying alliances with Russia and China.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Houthis tighten control of strategic Red Sea towns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35b4e3a035fe9fe5e3bdd26c1dc634657317fd5d34cc222282b9870a924f5d59</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthis-tighten-control-of-strategic-red-sea-towns/a-79220628--4b086e3863b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthis-tighten-control-of-strategic-red-sea-towns/a-79220628?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Reports indicate Houthi militants have taken over the port city of Mokha along with Perim Island, which occupies a strategic position on a vital transport waterway in the Red Sea.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turks in Germany anxious after AfD wins in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bda56ccb9b8cf8805648b59b2187ac525c35a62c51a368b1be4a7dd0289442af</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764--9bdd69d84853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party's win in Saxony-Anhalt has alarmed people of Turkish origin in eastern states. Will workers and business owners abandon the increasingly AfD-friendly region for the more welcoming west?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China angered by Taiwan VP's visit to EU democracy forum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02d942d1dc9f0a3a70b85a245f744e25e5bce4a6169fe58ccf102d2c9ea62e2a</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-angered-by-taiwan-vp-s-visit-to-eu-democracy-forum/a-79226311--51b6e60ff469.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-angered-by-taiwan-vp-s-visit-to-eu-democracy-forum/a-79226311?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing has lodged a complaint with Italy and the EU over top Taiwanese officials visiting a democracy conference. The EU is navigating contentious issues with China and high-ranking Taiwanese visits are rare.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The 'end of an era' as Goethe-Institut in Russia closes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7fc7376d063d3ee96757e83d4a41c679acd46e2be2368666e7f5dcffe493d5a</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321--189393464061.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Goethe-Institut was one of the last German institutions still operating in Russia. However, following Moscow's decision to close its offices, all employees will have to stop working by September 13.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Far right lead in upcoming state election polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03a3951c9040a401bb1507701e0a1d4df5bcab4ab2948c575639b07184545293</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-far-right-lead-in-upcoming-state-election-polls/live-79223427--90302ab1c910.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-far-right-lead-in-upcoming-state-election-polls/live-79223427?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Polling suggests the far-right AfD is carrying its momentum into another upcoming state election. Meanwhile, former Chancellor Angela Merkel has urged people not to take democracy for granted. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong Tiananmen activists jailed for up to 7 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23539a3efe7b3ecbe3ee2cbcdf7eed0b1c390a709ebdb8bd2dbf9bb31da946ca</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-tiananmen-activists-jailed-for-up-to-7-years/a-79224243--b40cd2f6f0ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-tiananmen-activists-jailed-for-up-to-7-years/a-79224243?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three pro-democracy activists who organized annual commemorations of China's deadly 1989 Tiananmen crackdown were charged under Hong Kong's Beijing-backed national security law.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Magyar vs. Moscow: Hungary's new tough stance toward Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:beb1d109251bd7f04715c220d61985e131e8c2a925f1a5337b022f6808a3e348</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/magyar-vs-moscow-hungary-s-new-tough-stance-toward-russia/a-79223424--11535ff26ff5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/magyar-vs-moscow-hungary-s-new-tough-stance-toward-russia/a-79223424?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungarian PM Peter Magyar has abruptly ended the era of his predecessor's warm relations with Russia: Budapest has expelled 10 Russian diplomats from the country. Moscow is considering halting gas supplies in response.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines ferry fire: Search continues for dozens missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06ec8fbff80029cb4171bc8f574a8510cf9b2cf9b781334c143ead0b08d06af5</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-ferry-fire-search-continues-for-dozens-missing/a-79223425--fc38c9af4128.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-ferry-fire-search-continues-for-dozens-missing/a-79223425?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Firefighters searching for survivors combed through the smoking remains of a ferry off the coast of Coron island in the Philippines. Five people died and over 40 have been rescued</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's connection to the 9/11 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:906dced0787da2a940588a14eb9fcf77743e955b056e97359a763defb3bf4902</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T06:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-9-11-attacks/a-79202918--33622f8e5007.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-9-11-attacks/a-79202918?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 9/11 plot, including the twin tower attacks, was partly planned by the so-called Hamburg cell. A look at how Germany's national security was reshaped.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>New California social media laws target addictive features</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cef5503be40a63bc50a679f5100d52200441030ba3ee5eb27639278d766c44a0</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T06:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-california-social-media-laws-target-addictive-features/a-79222996--2a8efa2b4a90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-california-social-media-laws-target-addictive-features/a-79222996?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several new laws are aimed at "psychologically exploitative" social media functions for children. Governor Gavin Newsom said the laws target the technology behind addictive use rather than age alone.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany sets its sights on Russia's shadow fleet</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b8929c0877ad3341eff1dca846bb3c75f8c63f9234f3dea36cad4aaf3e7f0e5</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T17:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-sets-its-sights-on-russia-s-shadow-fleet/a-79211123--786b113b7d97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-sets-its-sights-on-russia-s-shadow-fleet/a-79211123?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German government wants to follow other EU countries and take more decisive action against Russia's shadow fleet, accusing it of helping Moscow evade sanctions and carry out acts of sabotage.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Why are European banks moving their gold out of the US?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22138a946fb06f290fba64654d28c243b407cc2be507ad3efa9d23928d73ac88</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T05:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-are-european-banks-moving-their-gold-out-of-the-us/a-79213013--768a21b6850a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-are-european-banks-moving-their-gold-out-of-the-us/a-79213013?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Netherlands and France have moved their gold out of US vaults. Part of the reason is fear over US reliability, but equally important is the need to have their gold closer to home in the event of a crisis.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish lawmakers back citizenship for Sahrawis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ecfe6db771d83463fcff59f9774ea00c8d1adc36bf1c4d706138ecbb4db9c55</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T03:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spanish-lawmakers-back-citizenship-for-sahrawis/a-79222841--98a92dd37696.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spanish-lawmakers-back-citizenship-for-sahrawis/a-79222841?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spanish lawmakers approved a bill that could give citizenship to tens of thousands of Sahrawis and their descendants, amid tense ties with Morocco. The legislation must now pass the senate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Algeria cuts diplomatic ties with UAE</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b795c856334ecc2ae7cf6ea00498eaf4e4aa6e88f01b42dc34fb7dc0d025fcc</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T22:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/algeria-cuts-diplomatic-ties-with-uae/a-79222141--9a0191878148.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/algeria-cuts-diplomatic-ties-with-uae/a-79222141?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Algeria said that it was closing its airspace and severing ties with the United Arab Emirates. Algiers accuses Abu Dhabi of destabilizing countries such as Libya, Sudan and Mali.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Switzerland: Five killed in tourist bus crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2229b2024f4917b25894704282a39321cce8ea9d67b5a29a15cdcccf97b55fc</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/switzerland-five-killed-in-tourist-bus-crash/a-79221766--8a33d8e8bf35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/switzerland-five-killed-in-tourist-bus-crash/a-79221766?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A tourist coach crashed near the alpine village of Susch in Switzerland's eastern canton of Graubünden. Dutch media reported that the bus was carrying tourists from the Netherlands.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
